KZ3 patch 1127 (SPU pass 106): diagnostic environment switches on hot paths are read once instead of by a getenv on
every call. On Windows getenv takes the CRT lock and scans the environment linearly; upstream ps3recomp issue #243
measured one getenv in a hot SPU loop halving a title's fps. No behaviour change: each switch is still "set or not"
(or the same string) as before, read at its first use. Macros KZ3_ENV_ON(slot, name) (int slot, -1 = unread) and
KZ3_ENV_STR(slot, name) (const char* slot, (const char*)1 = unread), defined per file under #ifndef. ASSUMPTION: no
cached switch changes after the game starts (port/kz3/main.cpp's kz3_setenv/_putenv calls all run before ppu_run).
Sites (30 getenv calls):
  runtime/spu/spurs_job.c   spu_run_spurs_job: SPURS_JOB_DESCDUMP (2, level cached), SPURS_JOB_DUMP (2), per job
  runtime/spu/spu_lifted_job.h  spu_run_lifted_job_abi: SPURS_TASKSET_TRACE, SPU_WORKER_TRACE, per run
  runtime/spu/spu_channels.c    spu_run_with_halt: SPU_ARGWATCH, per run
  runtime/syscalls/sys_cond.c   sys_cond_wait: PS3_COND_PEEK, PS3_COND_SPURIOUS_MS, per wait
  runtime/syscalls/sys_event.c  sys_event_queue_receive: YDKJ_Q23STACK, PS3_EVT_RECV_TRACE; sys_event_port_send:
                                YDKJ_NO_PORTROUTE
  runtime/syscalls/lv2_register.c  spu_dispatch_frame_by_queue (every port send, empty-queue receive): RD_SPU_INTERP
                                (+ its group-start use); sys_tty_write: YDKJ_CRIBT, YDKJ_ASSERTBT, FLOW_PSSGTRACE
  runtime/syscalls/sys_semaphore.c wait/post: SEMTID (4), SEMCHAIN (2), PS3_SEMTRACE
  runtime/syscalls/sys_fs.c     sys_fs_open: FLOW_TITLEOPEN, FLOW_TITLEFIX; sys_fs_read: FLOW_FSDBG
  runtime/ppu/ppu_sysprx.cpp    sys_lwmutex_create / destroy: LWM_COUNT (2)
  runtime/ppu/ppu_loader.cpp    lv2_syscall's tty write: FLOW_PSSGTRACE
Not changed: getenv sites already cached, nid- or image-gated ones (ps3_hle_call's YDKJ_* blocks), error and init
paths. runtime/ppu/ppu_fs.cpp (cellFs HLE: 24 per-call getenv of FS_CALLER, PS3_FSLOG*, FS_READ_*, FS_STACK,
FS_FSTAT_CAP*) is left: patches 2078, 4017 and 4018 use those lines as context (kept on purpose).
libs/video (RSX, 2xxx) not audited here. Test: tools/spu/test_r106_getenv_once.sh. Upstream candidate
(cites #243).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): upstream 634871d1 read the same switches once: those hunks are upstream's now.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.19.0 (group B pass 2, R&C 2026-11-09, on KZ3's group A r152): builds on #515 (37b09103/6f590f42, ps3_env_once):
the spurs_job.c part is dropped (SPURS_JOB_DESCDUMP and SPURS_JOB_DUMP are read through upstream's ps3_env_once there).
The KZ3_ENV_ON/KZ3_ENV_STR caches in the nine files upstream did not convert are unchanged.
Pass 2: tools/test_lwmutex_semantics.py (refreshed by 1122) extracts handlers that now use KZ3_ENV_ON; its harness defines
KZ3_ENV_ON as 0 (switches off).

